ort_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/v0awz6","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/v0awz6/wonderful_wifi232_serial_wifi_bridge"},{"short_id":"ain4bf","created_at":"2017-06-04T14:30:23.000-05:00","title":"ELPI: Fast, Embeddable, Lamba-Prolog Interpreter (2015)","url":"http://www.cs.unibo.it/~sacerdot/PAPERS/elpi.pdf","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"nickpsecurity","user_is_author":false,"tags":["formalmethods","pdf","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ain4bf","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/ain4bf/elpi_fast_embeddable_lamba_prolog"},{"short_id":"k6mdan","created_at":"2017-06-04T14:29:33.000-05:00","title":"Jean Sammet, Co-Designer of COBOL, Dies at 89","url":"https://www.nytimes.com/2017/06/04/technology/obituary-jean-sammet-software-designer-cobol.html","score":11,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"aleph","user_is_author":false,"tags":["historical","person"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k6mdan","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/k6mdan/jean_sammet_co_designer_cobol_dies_at_89"},{"short_id":"d4ez7j","created_at":"2017-06-04T13:01:36.000-05:00","title":"The Strongtalk Type System for Smalltalk","url":"http://www.bracha.org/nwst.html","score":10,"flags":0,"comment_count":3,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"nickpsecurity","user_is_author":false,"tags":["programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/d4ez7j","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/d4ez7j/strongtalk_type_system_for_smalltalk"},{"short_id":"tpkowb","created_at":"2017-06-04T12:12:58.000-05:00","title":"I made a search engine to show the best paths for learning anything","url":"https://learn-anything.xyz/","score":45,"flags":0,"comment_count":13,"description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://learn-anything.xyz/\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eHere\u003c/a\u003e is the search engine. And \u003ca href=\"https://learn-anything.xyz/computer_science\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, for example is a mind map for learning computer science.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe idea is that a person can type what he wants to learn and the most efficient path to learning the topic is shown.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI \u003ca href=\"https://lobste.rs/s/flcfgl/mind_map_knowledge_study_plan_for\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ealways wanted to build a search engine\u003c/a\u003e that shows the most efficient paths to \u003ca href=\"https://learn-anything.github.io/future/2017/05/27/future-of-learning.html\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003elearn anything in a linear way\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe most awesome thing is that if anyone thinks there is a better way to learn any of the topics, one can say it since it is an \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nikitavoloboev/learn-anything\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003eopen source project\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWould love to hear your thoughts on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"[Here](https://learn-anything.xyz/) is the search engine. And [here](https://learn-anything.xyz/computer_science), for example is a mind map for learning computer science.\r\n\r\nThe idea is that a person can type what he wants to learn and the most efficient path to learning the topic is shown.\r\n\r\nI [always wanted to build a search engine](https://lobste.rs/s/flcfgl/mind_map_knowledge_study_plan_for) that shows the most efficient paths to [learn anything in a linear way](https://learn-anything.github.io/future/2017/05/27/future-of-learning.html).\r\n\r\nThe most awesome thing is that if anyone thinks there is a better way to learn any of the topics, one can say it since it is an [open source project](https://github.com/nikitavoloboev/learn-anything). \r\n\r\nWould love to hear your thoughts on it.","submitter_user":"nikivi","user_is_author":true,"tags":["compsci","education","show"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tpkowb","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/tpkowb/i_made_search_engine_show_best_paths_for"},{"short_id":"upoeur","created_at":"2017-06-04T11:46:06.000-05:00","title":"Rosetta - A Solver-aided Programming Language That Extends Racket","url":"https://emina.github.io/rosette/index.html","score":15,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"nickpsecurity","user_is_author":false,"tags":["compsci","formalmethods","lisp","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/upoeur","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/upoeur/rosetta_solver_aided_programming"},{"short_id":"pdy68r","created_at":"2017-06-04T11:19:58.000-05:00","title":"Testing Distributed Systems for Linearizability","url":"http://www.anishathalye.com/2017/06/04/testing-distributed-systems-for-linearizability/","score":9,"flags":0,"comment_count":8,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"anishathalye","user_is_author":true,"tags":["distributed","testing"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/pdy68r","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/pdy68r/testing_distributed_systems_for"},{"short_id":"acnzrg","created_at":"2017-06-04T09:01:41.000-05:00","title":"Differences between tmux vs screen","url":"https://wtanaka.com/node/8136","score":25,"flags":0,"comment_count":18,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"mulander","user_is_author":false,"tags":["programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/acnzrg","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/acnzrg/differences_between_tmux_vs_screen"},{"short_id":"m5qyij","created_at":"2017-06-04T07:48:57.000-05:00","title":"Understanding the “GPL is a Contract” court case","url":"https://perens.com/blog/2017/05/28/understanding-the-gpl-is-a-contract-court-case/","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"pizzaiolo","user_is_author":false,"tags":["law"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m5qyij","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/m5qyij/understanding_gpl_is_contract_court_case"},{"short_id":"gpc49c","created_at":"2017-06-04T06:42:44.000-05: